# Targeting through the real keys (owner, 2026-09-16): every body carries its
# wordless tag; holding Z locks the nearest threat, leans the camera in behind
# the player and reads the body on the slate; u and o (or the scroll) cycle the
# lock, never the move keys, so a strafe keeps it; r sweeps
# the whole field and stands the camera back; letting go puts it all away. And
# a fight is fought with the key held.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/targeting.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --folk=8
coast calm
wait 0.8

# --- a body, and the tag it carries without anybody asking -----------------------
spawn runner
wait 0.8
shot 01-a-machine-carries-its-tag with mob:runner

# --- the lock: the camera leans in and the slate reads it -------------------------
hold target
await target 5
await target_lean 5
wait 0.9
shot 02-locked-the-camera-leans with mob:runner

# --- another body, and the lock cycled onto it ------------------------------------
spawn cutter
wait 0.6
shot 03-a-second-machine with mob:cutter,mob:runner
tap target_next
wait 0.5
await target 3
shot 04-cycled-to-another with mob:cutter,mob:runner

# --- the field swept: the camera stands back and every body is read ---------------
tap ability_scan
await target_sweep 5
wait 0.9
shot 05-the-field-swept with mob:runner,mob:cutter
tap ability_scan
wait 0.5
await target 3

# --- a fight, with the key still held ---------------------------------------------
walkto part 6
press swing
await hit 6
wait 0.3
shot 06-fought-while-reading with mob:runner

# --- let go: the camera comes back square and the reads go ------------------------
release target
await target_none 5
wait 1.2
shot 07-let-go-and-square with mob:runner

# --- a village, and a field bigger than one page ----------------------------------
# One of the last people is read as a person: no health, no signature, just who
# they are and what they are doing. A person always sorts below everything in the
# fight, so one step BACK from a fresh lock wraps onto them, however many machines
# are about. And with the village's own people and the eight the tour boots with
# (--folk=8), the field runs past a single page: the gap this closes is a sweep
# that stopped at eight and never said there were more.
village 0
wait 2.5
hold target
await target 8
tap target_prev
wait 0.6
await target_person 8
shot 08-a-person-read-as-a-person with folk
tap ability_scan
await target_sweep 5
await target_paged 5
wait 0.6
shot 09-a-field-on-two-pages with folk
tap target_next
wait 0.6
shot 10-the-second-page with folk
release target
await target_none 5
